{{!--
  UXReviewRecord -- fm-web's second UX-heavy template (19 §19.1). Same conventions as
  component-spec.md.hbs's own doc comment: real 19 §19.2 TemplateContext, built-in helpers only,
  triple-stash throughout, "[]"-on-empty for every array field. `findings` is `.min(1)`-shaped in
  ux-review-record.schema.json, so the fixture context this template is tested against always supplies
  at least one -- the {{else}} branch below exists only so a caller passing a genuinely empty list gets
  a template that still emits valid, parseable YAML (an empty key, not a schema-breaking null), the
  schema's own minItems check then correctly refusing the result rather than this template silently
  producing invalid front matter.
--}}
---
id: {{{artifact.id}}}
type: UXReviewRecord
schemaVersion: 1
title: UX review -- {{{inputs.subject}}}
status: draft
created: {{{now}}}
updated: {{{now}}}
revision: 1
author: {{{artifact.author}}}
changelog: []
subject: {{{inputs.subject}}}
severity: {{{inputs.severity}}}
findings:
{{#each inputs.findings}}
  - {{{this}}}
{{else}}
  []
{{/each}}
recommendation: {{{inputs.recommendation}}}
---

# UX review: {{{inputs.subject}}}

Reviewed by **{{{artifact.author}}}** for **{{{project.name}}}**. Overall severity:
**{{{inputs.severity}}}**.

## Findings

{{#each inputs.findings}}
- {{{this}}}
{{else}}
_No findings recorded._
{{/each}}

## Recommendation

{{{inputs.recommendation}}}
